From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 013/NNN] srslog: fall back to process accounting for RUSAGE_THREAD

Darwin accounts resource usage per process and has no RUSAGE_THREAD. The
benchmark falls back to RUSAGE_SELF, which counts context switches across
the whole process and therefore overstates the figure this benchmark is
measuring. That is recorded in a comment at the definition.

--- a/lib/test/srslog/benchmarks/frontend_latency.cpp	2026-09-03 15:15:56
+++ b/lib/test/srslog/benchmarks/frontend_latency.cpp	2026-09-03 15:16:17
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
 #include "srsran/srslog/srslog.h"
 #include <atomic>
 #include <sys/resource.h>
+
+#ifndef RUSAGE_THREAD
+/* Darwin accounts resource usage per process, not per thread. The counts
+ * become process wide, which overstates this benchmark's context switches. */
+#define RUSAGE_THREAD RUSAGE_SELF
+#endif
 #include <thread>
 
 using namespace srslog;
